title: Parity audit, visual approval, and what stays deferred
---
date: 2026-10-18
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: A row-by-row audit closes milestone eight, the owner passes visual approval, and unverified live services are recorded as deferred rather than passed.
---
tags: release, documentation, interface
---
source_commit: 0487709e3fa764a3bd7ce3e357b67f802f1d80b4
---
body:

The final parity milestone was an audit rather than a feature. A row-by-row
acceptance document compares the implementation with the reference and states
each disposition, including compatibility limits. Fixes from the audit added a
bounded converter for the reference application's export format, vendored math
and syntax highlighting, accessible in-app dialogs, and the dashboard layout.

Browser checks used disposable loopback databases only, with no real inference
or search calls. They covered file choosers, exports, deletion and discard
confirmations, folder ordering with a deliberately stale second tab, and layouts
at full-window and side-panel widths with no horizontal overflow. Native browser
confirmation dialogs repeatedly stalled the test driver, so decisions use HTML
dialogs instead.

The owner then passed visual approval for the current V0-2-0 interface and
deferred verification against real embedding, search, and summarizer services.
Both statuses are recorded exactly: approval is not pixel-equality proof, and
the deferral is not a pass or a waiver. Provider authentication, Strata
cold-start checks, and final Phase 1 sign-off remain deferred until V2-0-0.

[Commit 0487709](https://github.com/Labyricorn/Labbonet/commit/0487709e3fa764a3bd7ce3e357b67f802f1d80b4)
